# Cloudflare Workers AI (edge-served open models)
# The same CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID also configure
# Cloudflare Clef (the `decide` inference type); see the block near the end of
# this file. Commented out, unlike the keys around them: values copied from here
# unedited would be sent to Cloudflare as a real token, and with them built-in
# features would start sending their decision requests there (and the
# classifier router's auto mode would switch to decisions), each one failing
# with a 401.
# Token must have Workers AI Read+Write scope
# CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY=your-cloudflare-api-token
# REQUIRED: account id from https://dash.cloudflare.com (URL or 'Account ID' panel)
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your-cloudflare-account-id
# Optional: CLOUDFLARE_MODEL=@cf/meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct-fp8-fast

