# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TypeSafe (Jev) — the `decide` inference type: typed, calibrated decisions.
# Either TYPESAFE_API_KEY or AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY (the Vercel AI Gateway route,
# below) configures it, and nothing else is needed: NeuroLink then uses Jev for
# the internal decisions that have no opt-in of their own (context compaction),
# and silently keeps its previous behaviour when no key is present or the key is
# rejected. Model routing, tool routing and RAG planning stay opt-in even with a
# key (classifierRouter.enabled with a pool, toolRouting.enabled, a decide
# function passed to a RAGPipeline); the key does not switch them on.
# Get a key at https://console.typesafe.ai/keys
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=your-typesafe-api-key
# TYPESAFE_MODEL=jev-latest
# TYPESAFE_BASE_URL=https://api.typesafe.ai
#
# The same model is also reachable through the Vercel AI Gateway. Create a key
# under Vercel -> your team -> AI Gateway -> API Keys. Note the gateway will not
# serve ANY request until that team has a credit card on file (even for the free
# credits): a valid key on a card-less team returns 403
# customer_verification_required, which is an account state, not a bad key.
# Holding both keys keeps the direct transport, because only it reports the
# vendor's own calibrated confidence; the gateway's is derived.
# TYPESAFE_TRANSPORT=direct|gateway   # optional override
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=vck_...
# TYPESAFE_GATEWAY_URL=https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v4/ai/evaluation-model   # optional override of the gateway route

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Laya — an open-weights decision model (the `decide` inference type). There
# is no built-in endpoint: LAYA_BASE_URL is required, pointing at a Laya server
# or a LiteLLM pass-through route to one (NeuroLink calls <base>/predict). On
# LiteLLM, the key needs that route in its Allowed Routes. Built-in features
# use Laya only when neither TYPESAFE_API_KEY nor AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY is set
# (both are TypeSafe keys); otherwise only where a caller asks for "laya".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LAYA_BASE_URL=https://your-proxy.example.com/laya
# LAYA_API_KEY=sk-your-key
# LAYA_MODEL=typed-decisions   # english | multilingual | typed-decisions | auto

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# XOR — an open-weights decision model that also reads images and video (the
# `decide` inference type). There is no built-in endpoint: XOR_BASE_URL is
# required, pointing at an XOR deployment or a LiteLLM pass-through route to
# one (NeuroLink calls <base>/v1/systemone). On LiteLLM, the key's team must
# allow the model. Built-in features use XOR only when neither TypeSafe nor
# Laya is configured (TypeSafe counts with either of its two keys, Laya only with
# its key and its base URL); otherwise only where a caller asks for "xor".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# XOR_BASE_URL=https://your-proxy.example.com   # https:// (http:// only for localhost / 127.0.0.1 / [::1])
# XOR_API_KEY=sk-your-key
# XOR_MODEL=xor-1.1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Perplexity Decisions API — a decision model that also reads images (the
# `decide` inference type, model pplx-decider-v1-27b). Hosted at
# https://api.perplexity.ai, so the key alone configures it (NeuroLink calls
# <base>/v1/decisions). PERPLEXITY_API_KEY is the SAME variable the Perplexity
# text provider (Sonar) reads: setting it for that provider also lets built-in
# features use this one when no other decision provider is configured. They
# are tried in this order: TypeSafe, Laya, XOR, then Perplexity; naming
# "perplexity-decider" reaches it directly. The key itself is the
# PERPLEXITY_API_KEY set in the Perplexity Sonar block above.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PERPLEXITY_DECIDER_BASE_URL=https://api.perplexity.ai   # optional override of the origin
# PERPLEXITY_DECIDER_MODEL=pplx-decider-v1-27b

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare Clef — decision models that also read images (the `decide`
# inference type; models clef, 27B, and clef-flash, 9B), served by Workers AI.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_KEY and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID are the SAME variables the
# Cloudflare Workers AI text provider reads (see above, where they are commented
# out): setting them for that provider also lets built-in features use Clef when
# no other decision provider is configured. They are tried in this order: TypeSafe, Laya, XOR, Perplexity,
# then Cloudflare Clef; naming "cloudflare-clef" reaches it directly. The Workers AI
# endpoint ignored text past about 2,048 tokens until 2026-10-04 and read far more
# on 2026-10-07 (hosted service or model: unknown). NeuroLink refuses a state it
# estimates at more than 16,000 tokens, and caps the encoded request at 256,000
# bytes, base64 image data included.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLOUDFLARE_CLEF_BASE_URL=https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4   # optional override
# CLOUDFLARE_CLEF_MODEL=clef

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which decision provider built-in features use. Unset: the first configured
# one, in the order TypeSafe, Laya, XOR, Perplexity, Cloudflare Clef. `none`
# turns the default off, so a PERPLEXITY_API_KEY set for Sonar, or a Cloudflare
# token set for Workers AI text, sends no decision requests. A provider's name
# (typesafe, laya, xor, perplexity-decider, cloudflare-clef) pins the default to
# that one while it is configured and never falls back to another. A call that
# names a provider (`provider:` / `--provider`) is not affected.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEUROLINK_DECISION_PROVIDER=none
